The following are the top ten most threatened species in Canada, according to a report by WWF (World Wildlife Fund) Canada’s Living Planet Report Card for Freshwater Species released last week at an event hosted by MP John Aldag in Vancouver.

The list includes:

* Pacific salmon – including Chinook, coho, chum, sockeye, pink;
* Lake sturgeon;
* Paddlefish;
* Longnose sucker;
* Shorthead redhorse;
* Flathead chub;
* White river spring snail;
* Western painted turtle;
* Yellowfin madtom;
* Spotted gar.
